 "traditions": [],
 "notes": "Planned kind 'Other fortified wine' is kept as 'Regional fortified wine' (the checker bars 'Other …' names); its old models are kept (Morris under Rutherglen Muscat; Bodegas de Alberto Dorado stays in m because no page I retrieved describes Rueda dorado, and the Rueda DO page does not mention it). Marsala moved out of the catch-all into its own kind; the generic old model 'Marsala' (no maker) was dropped. Near-duplicate old entries were merged: Lustau PX VORS (two spellings) and D'Oliveiras Malvazia 1991 (two spellings). Ferreira Dona Antonia and Lustau East India Solera stay in m because no retrieved page gave their style. Montilla-Moriles is included as the plan asks, though its page says the wines are usually not fortified. Not added: Rutherglen producers other than Morris, Banyuls/Maury estates, Madeira 20–50 year categories, sherry 12/15-year labels, Málaga and Mavrodaphne (no retrieved page). Pages that failed: Wikipedia Taylor's_(port) and Quinta_do_Noval (404), wein.plus (401), Wikidata (429). Brands for Dow's, Cockburn's, Fonseca and Croft are cited to group pages that only list them; founding years left blank where not on a retrieved page."
}